// result_end
\caption(Actual pilot and leaf locations for the smaller diagnostic run.)
\alttext(Blue leaf samples enter the estimator; red pilots guide adaptation and are discarded from the final estimate.)

> Retain the original sixteen-seed comparison

The original budgets2000,5000,10000,20000,50000,100000 and sixteen replicates
are retained. MISER uses its xorshift seeds1..16. Plain Monte Carlo preserves
the original MT19937-64 seeds1001..1016 and uniform_real_distribution. These are
distinct sampling designs, not paired identical random streams. Each method
makes exactly the same requested number of integrand evaluations per replicate,
including MISER pilots.

The figure expresses RMS error in units of one-millionth of an integral unit,
while the table retains unscaled values. The finite-replicate RMS error compares
estimates against the analytic finite-box integral. A smaller observed RMS on
this peak is evidence for this experiment, not proof of universal dominance,
unbiased estimated variance, or an improved asymptotic exponent. No timing
comparison is made.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/miser_comparison.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto rows =
        dm::algorithms::miser_gaussian_comparison({2000, 5000, 10000, 20000,
                                                   50000, 100000});
    std::vector<double> x, m, pv;
    std::print("| actual calls per method/run | replicates | MISER RMS error | original plain RMS error " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : rows) {
        x.push_back(r.calls);
        m.push_back(r.miser_rms * 1e6);
        pv.push_back(r.plain_rms * 1e6);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.calls, r.replicates,
                   r.miser_rms, r.plain_rms);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, m, "MISER observed RMS", {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(
        x, pv, "plain observed RMS", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title(
        "Original Gaussian: finite 16-seed RMS comparison").x_label(
        "actual evaluations per run").y_label("RMS error (1e-6 integral units)").save_svg("build/miser_comparison.svg");
}
```
