> Count pilot overhead explicitly

The next trace sweep separates pilot calls from retained leaf calls. Their sum
is the exact budget. Smaller boxes inherit their actual recursion budgets, so
counting only final samples would understate MISER's evaluation cost. Root and
child records retain the selected axis and actual pilot standard deviations as
well as their allocations.

The native reported variance sums leaf estimates V squared times(mean(f
squared)−mean(f) squared)/n, clipped at zero. This population-variance plug-in
is biased at finite n and can suffer cancellation; it is not an unbiased
variance estimate or guaranteed error bar. Nonfinite callbacks, squared values,
geometry or returned statistics throw. Invalid boxes and budgets below two throw
before any callback, correcting the legacy behavior of silently spending two
calls for smaller requests.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/miser_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, pilot, leaf;
    std::print("| requested calls | actual evaluations | actual pilots | actual retained leaf calls | " "recursion nodes |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (long n : {32L, 63L, 64L, 65L, 128L, 256L, 512L, 1024L, 2048L}) {
        auto t =
            dm::algorithms::miser_trace(dm::algorithms::miser_gaussian, {0, 0},
                                        {1, 1}, n, 1);
        std::size_t pilots = 0;
        for (auto &r : t.nodes)
            pilots += r.pilot_calls;
        x.push_back(n);
        pilot.push_back(pilots);
        leaf.push_back(t.evaluations - pilots);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, t.evaluations, pilots,
                   t.evaluations - pilots, t.nodes.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, pilot, "actual discarded pilots", {220, 38, 38}, 2).line(
        x, leaf, "actual retained leaf calls", {37, 99, 235}, 2).title(
        "MISER: actual evaluation-budget composition").x_label(
        "requested evaluations").y_label("actual callback calls").save_svg(
        "build/miser_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| requested calls | actual evaluations | actual pilots | actual retained leaf calls | recursion nodes |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 32 | 32 | 0 | 32 | 1 |
| 63 | 63 | 0 | 63 | 1 |
| 64 | 64 | 16 | 48 | 3 |
| 65 | 65 | 16 | 49 | 3 |
| 128 | 128 | 32 | 96 | 5 |
| 256 | 256 | 76 | 180 | 9 |
| 512 | 512 | 225 | 287 | 17 |
| 1024 | 1024 | 490 | 534 | 31 |
| 2048 | 2048 | 1103 | 945 | 53 |
\image(figures/miser_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Exact budget composition at and around the split threshold.)
\alttext(Pilot and leaf counts sum to the requested number; splitting begins at64 calls.)

> Capture contract, conclusion and references

The trace owns original bounds, region bounds and all actual callback
values/coordinates. Capture units count original2d bounds, each region record
plus2d bounds, and each sample record plus d coordinates. The optional quota
defaults to1000000; zero disables. Actual admission occurs before the next
stored evaluation or region; earlier callback side effects remain if a later
quota or callback fails. There is no partial returned trace. Ordinary work is
O(d times calls) excluding callback cost; trace storage is proportional to
actual captured units.

The constant example validates accounting, the original peak illustrates
adaptive placement, and replicated errors describe a finite comparison. The
mathematical allocation objective explains why adaptation can help without
promising that noisy pilot estimates always choose well.

[Press and Farrar, Recursive stratified sampling for multidimensional Monte Carlo integration (1990)|https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4822899]
introduces MISER. The fixed pilot fraction, original stream, clipping and exact
budget contracts specify this implementation.

> Verification

The ten-report batch passes95 CTest cases,31 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,83 compiled and executed public examples,363/363 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python integer
arithmetic, MT19937-64/variation replay, graph sets, analytic interpolation,
circle boundary enumeration and actual-sample integration reconstruction agree
on915459 captured records. All six original RMS summaries are separately checked
using96 native MISER estimates and1600000 independently reproduced
plain-comparator points. Frozen valid-input comparisons include the original
seeded solver paths and full MOEA/D fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten
identically installed development headers compile independently, and an
installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each report has four executed
complete programs, four reviewed native figures and both HTML/Markdown exports
with computed-result and image-byte checks. This is a scoped native API audit,
not an installation claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-234-243/`.
